[ti:Grandfather's Clock]
[ar:Henry Clay Work]
[00:00.00]My grandfather's clock was too large for the shelf
[00:26.00]So it stood ninety years on the floor
[00:41.00]It was taller by half than the old man himself
[00:53.00]Though it weighed not a pennyweight more
[01:00.00]It was bought on the morn of the day that he was born
[01:12.00]And was always his treasure and pride
[01:18.00]But it stopped short, never to go again
[01:25.00]When the old man died
